1640
00:50:29,310 --> 00:50:32,070
while the capacity can be made larger and larger.

1641
00:50:32,070 --> 00:50:35,170
And its cost can also be made lower and lower.

1642
00:50:35,170 --> 00:50:40,710
So this is the hierarchy of our storage devices.

1643
00:50:40,710 --> 00:50:42,390
Now, from a programmer's point of view,

1644
00:50:42,390 --> 00:50:44,330
the reason we understand this hierarchy

1645
00:50:44,330 --> 00:50:47,470
is mainly in the process of developing programs,

1646
00:50:47,470 --> 00:50:50,870
so that our programs run fast,

1647
00:50:50,870 --> 00:50:53,890
we can take the data we operate on frequently

1648
00:50:53,890 --> 00:50:57,170
and place it as close to our processor as possible,

1649
00:50:57,170 --> 00:51:00,930
for example in memory, cache, or registers.

1650
00:51:00,930 --> 00:51:05,450
That way, our programs can run very fast.

1651
00:51:05,450 --> 00:51:08,470
This is a kind of optimization technique.

1652
00:51:08,470 --> 00:51:11,430
So I hope everyone

1653
00:51:11,430 --> 00:51:14,870
can also get an understanding of this diagram.

1654
00:51:14,870 --> 00:51:18,890
This is the hierarchy of storage devices.

1655
00:51:18,890 --> 00:51:24,570
The last part, as the final section of this chapter,

1656
00:51:24,570 --> 00:51:25,710
the last part,

1657
00:51:25,710 --> 00:51:31,970
as an important part of our entire computer system,

1658
00:51:31,970 --> 00:51:32,610
is the operating system.

1659
00:51:32,610 --> 00:51:34,110
This is also an important topic

1660
00:51:34,110 --> 00:51:39,670
that I hope everyone will study in this course.

1661
00:51:39,670 --> 00:51:42,050
So this is our last operating system.

1662
00:51:42,050 --> 00:51:44,930
Now, as for this operating system,

1663
00:51:44,930 --> 00:51:46,950
we know that in

1664
00:51:46,950 --> 00:51:49,530
in our entire

1665
00:51:49,530 --> 00:51:52,510
computer system,

1666
00:51:52,510 --> 00:51:55,590
at the very bottom we have our hardware,

1667
00:51:55,590 --> 00:51:58,610
and at the very top we have our software.

1668
00:51:58,610 --> 00:52:00,970
Now, as software developed,

1669
00:52:00,970 --> 00:52:02,870
software split into two parts:

1670
00:52:02,870 --> 00:52:04,950
one part is the operating system,

1671
00:52:04,950 --> 00:52:06,750
and the other part is application programs.

1672
00:52:06,750 --> 00:52:09,350
Now, between the operating system and the application programs,

1673
00:52:09,350 --> 00:52:13,070
there is an interface.

1674
00:52:13,070 --> 00:52:14,130
And this interface,

1675
00:52:14,130 --> 00:52:16,150
we call system calls.

1676
00:52:16,150 --> 00:52:19,090
And between our operating system and the hardware,

1677
00:52:19,090 --> 00:52:21,270
there is also a layer of interface.

1678
00:52:21,270 --> 00:52:22,250
And this layer of interface,

1679
00:52:22,250 --> 00:52:24,190
we call the instruction set architecture.

1680
00:52:24,190 --> 00:52:26,790
So the instruction set architecture,

1681
00:52:26,790 --> 00:52:31,170
which is also what we'll cover in detail in the next chapter

1682
00:52:31,170 --> 00:52:33,790
Now, the operating system,

1683
00:52:33,790 --> 00:52:36,190
which is the main focus of this course,

1684
00:52:36,190 --> 00:52:39,370
its main functions

1685
00:52:39,370 --> 00:52:42,170
can be boiled down to two.

1686
00:52:42,170 --> 00:52:45,910
The first is to protect the hardware from being abused

1687
00:52:45,910 --> 00:52:46,890
by out-of-control software applications and programs.

1688
00:52:46,890 --> 00:52:52,250
Because if we let applications access hardware directly,

1689
00:52:52,250 --> 00:52:57,510
given varying levels of programmer skill,

1690
00:52:57,510 --> 00:53:01,070
or unexpected exceptions in a program,

1691
00:53:01,070 --> 00:53:03,030
the hardware could be damaged.

1692
00:53:03,030 --> 00:53:04,790
So one of the operating system's main functions

1693
00:53:04,790 --> 00:53:06,370
is to

1694
00:53:06,370 --> 00:53:09,390
prevent applications from accessing hardware directly,

1695
00:53:09,390 --> 00:53:10,830
and instead go through our system calls,

1696
00:53:10,830 --> 00:53:13,770
with the operating system accessing the hardware on their behalf,

1697
00:53:13,770 --> 00:53:17,790
so the operating system serves to protect the hardware.

1698
00:53:17,790 --> 00:53:20,150
On the other hand, going upward,

1699
00:53:20,150 --> 00:53:24,170
it provides applications with a simple, consistent abstraction interface,

1700
00:53:24,170 --> 00:53:25,410
which is exactly the system call.

1701
00:53:25,410 --> 00:53:31,050
so that applications can access the operating system through system calls,

1702
00:53:31,050 --> 00:53:33,990
and thereby indirectly access our hardware.

1703
00:53:33,990 --> 00:53:39,540
Alright, for today's class,

1704
00:53:39,540 --> 00:53:40,940
that's all I'll cover for you.
